        {
          "id": 2807617850,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The other APIs allow all negative values for  only, because those are containers for other fields that usually should throw exceptions on the subfields.\n\nOtherwise, -1 is only allowed for STRINGZ and VARINT where the length is deduced from the data, but those shouldn't be changed later.\n\nI would think setting to a negative value here should be limited to FT_PROTOCOL and FT_NONE. Do you have another use case?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
