        {
          "id": 2807631638,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The easiest fix is of course to not allow length < 0. I don't have any use cases, other than we had some Lua code which did not check the length before calling `set_len()`. In that specific case it was correct to set length to length_remaining, so instead of adding extra checks it would be nice if `set_len()` didn't fail.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
