      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2807654424,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Negative offsets and lengths are a bit of a pain, as it requires extra handling for 32-bit unsigned values that are used as offsets or lengths.\n\nThat's why I added the `tvb_new_subset_remaining()` and `tvb_new_subset_length()` routines, with the ultimate goal being to replace all cases where either length passed to other subset-tvb-creating routines is -1 meaning \"to the end\".\n\nSo maybe add `proto_item_set_len_remaining()`, or \"proto_item_set_len_all_remaining()`, or something such as that?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
